I used to live in an old house near power lines, and even with a battery 
backup/surge protector, I had all kinds of computer problems. Any 
long-lived character I had would end up dying to "a trickery"--what the 
game calls unrecoverable file corruption. So I backed up save files 
regularly.

I never had a serious impulse to restore a game where a character had 
died in-game. I don't even get the point of doing so: Nethack is 
essentially a solitaire game--the only one who knows you won knows how 
you did it. It would have felt cheap.

